    "### Handling Missing Values in Key Variables\n",
    "After restricting the dataset to relevant variables, missingness is significantly reduced and concentrated in a few key fields.\n",
    "In particular, the price variable exhibits substantial missingness in Copenhagen (approximately 41%), compared to a lower proportion in Rome (approximately 11%).\n",
    "Given the central role of price in the analysis, observations with missing price values are removed. While this reduces the sample size—especially for Copenhagen—it avoids introducing bias from unreliable imputations.\n",
    "Missing values in reviews_per_month are retained, as they likely reflect new or inactive listings rather than data quality issues.\n",
    "The variable estimated_revenue_l365d is also retained, but interpreted with caution, as it is derived rather than directly observed.\n",
    "\n",
    "The removal of observations with missing price values results in a substantial reduction of the Copenhagen dataset (approximately 41% of observations). This introduces a potential selection bias, as the remaining sample may not be fully representative of the original market.\n",
    "However, given the central role of price in the analysis and the lack of reliable imputation strategies, this trade-off is considered acceptable to preserve analytical validity."
   ]
